@startuml
title Student Feature — Sequence Diagram
autonumber

actor Student
participant "Student Web UI" as UI
participant "Student HTTP / Service" as StudentApi
participant "Student Draft Socket" as DraftSocket
participant "Student Presence / Failover\n(planned)" as Presence
participant "Foundation Query / State" as Foundation
participant "Teacher Backend" as Teacher
participant "StudentTrustedEndCoordinator\n(T004 proposal)" as EndCoordinator
participant "Foundation Lifecycle Transaction" as Lifecycle
participant "Student Winner Resolver" as WinnerResolver
database "Shared SQLite\n(same Database instance)" as DB

== Activity lookup and enrollment ==
Student -> UI : enter Activity Code
UI -> Foundation : GET /sessions/by-code/{code}
Foundation -> DB : resolve Session summary
DB --> Foundation : Session ID and phase
Foundation --> UI : minimal summary
UI -> StudentApi : GET student/join-options/{code}
StudentApi -> Foundation : reuse lookup + rate-limit semantics
StudentApi -> DB : list existing Team IDs/names only
DB --> StudentApi : selectable existing Teams
StudentApi --> UI : phase and join choices
Student -> UI : choose existing Team and display name
UI -> StudentApi : POST enrollment (same-origin Origin)
StudentApi -> StudentApi : validate input, Origin and rate limit;\nrequire CSRF for already-bound Session
StudentApi -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE
StudentApi -> DB : validate Session/Team; create/reuse credential and Participant mapping
StudentApi -> DB : insert TeamLeader only if none
DB --> StudentApi : committed Participant/Team/leader
StudentApi --> UI : membership + CSRF token; Set-Cookie HttpOnly
note over Student,StudentApi
First-time enrollment remains allowed after first Active, into an existing Team only.
This is not an existing Participant changing Teams; Student never creates Teams.
end note

== Activity state and target ==
note over UI,Foundation
The browser sends the Student-specific HttpOnly `student_session` cookie to both
Student HTTP and same-origin /socket.io because Path=/.
Student uses a WebSocket upgrade through Vite's proxy. The server validates
handshake Origin and resolves Participant/Team from the cookie mapping.
end note
UI -> Foundation : existing session:watch
Foundation -> Foundation : verify cookie-derived ActorContext
Foundation --> UI : current SessionStateSnapshot
Foundation --> UI : later session:state:changed after state commit
alt Waiting or no Round
  UI -> UI : show waiting; do not request target content
else Active
  UI -> Foundation : GET current-target
  Foundation -> DB : validate current Round and fetch target/Blanks
  Foundation --> UI : dynamic Question/QuestionGroup/Blank data
end

== Shared Team/Round draft ==
UI -> DraftSocket : student:draft:watch {sessionId, roundId}
DraftSocket -> DB : resolve credential, Team membership and Active Round
DraftSocket -> DB : read/create Team × Round draft
DB --> DraftSocket : latest persisted version and answers
DraftSocket --> UI : student:draft:snapshot
Student -> UI : edit a Blank
alt Student UI uses acknowledged HTTP edit
  UI -> StudentApi : PUT draft answer + CSRF + mutation ID
  StudentApi -> DB : shared DraftService immediate transaction; validate and persist edit/version
  DB --> StudentApi : committed change
  StudentApi --> DraftSocket : publish committed change to authorized Team/Round subscribers
  DraftSocket --> UI : student:draft:changed
  StudentApi --> UI : accepted change HTTP response
else supported Socket edit path
UI -> DraftSocket : student:draft:edit + CSRF token + mutation ID
DraftSocket -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE; validate actor/target/unlocked draft
DraftSocket -> DB : upsert Blank; increment version; COMMIT
DB --> DraftSocket : committed version/value
DraftSocket --> UI : student:draft:changed to server-derived Team/Round room
end
note over UI,DraftSocket
Same-Blank conflict: last server-accepted edit wins.
Refresh/reconnect uses persisted snapshot; Foundation state events carry no answers.
The UI serializes writes per Blank and retains focused/unsaved input.
Remote differences are indicated; submission waits for saved authoritative values.
end note

== Leader disconnect and role recovery (planned) ==
UI -> Presence : authenticated activity and draft sockets connect
UI -> Presence : F5 or other transport disconnect
Presence -> Presence : remove socket ID and check other valid sockets
alt current leader lost last valid socket
  Presence -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE; recheck leader and scope
  Presence -> DB : select first eligible online teammate by join order
  alt eligible candidate exists
    Presence -> DB : conditionally replace assignment; COMMIT
    Presence --> UI : student:membership:changed to affected Team's connected clients
  else no candidate
    Presence -> DB : keep assignment; no notification
  end
else other valid socket remains or actor is no longer leader
  Presence -> Presence : no leader change
end
UI -> StudentApi : GET /me on reconnect or membership invalidation
StudentApi -> DB : resolve same Cookie identity and current assignment
StudentApi --> UI : Participant / Team / current isLeader
note over UI,Presence
No application grace period. Reconnection does not reclaim a replaced role.
Disable submit until current role is resolved; preserve the draft.
end note

== Submission ==
Student -> UI : submit complete answers (leader only)
UI -> StudentApi : POST submission (answers confirm draft; no Team, role or acceptedOrder)
StudentApi -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE
StudentApi -> DB : revalidate leader, Active/current Round, exact target Blanks and no prior Submission
StudentApi -> DB : load authoritative draft; reject mismatched request confirmation
StudentApi -> DB : assign next acceptedOrder; insert Submission/draft answers; increment version and lock draft
DB --> StudentApi : committed Submission + locked draft
StudentApi --> UI : accepted outcome for this Team
StudentApi --> DraftSocket : publish student:draft:locked after commit

== Proposed Submission / End serialization (pending T004) ==
note over Teacher,Lifecycle
Teacher authorization, Coordinator and Foundation callback wiring are pending review.
Student Winner Resolver is implemented and tested independently.
end note
alt Submission gets SQLite write lock first
  Student -> StudentApi : concurrent valid submission
  StudentApi -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE; validate Active; persist Submission + lock draft; COMMIT
  Teacher -> EndCoordinator : endRound(input, trusted ActorContext)
  EndCoordinator -> EndCoordinator : verify teacher scope + round:end capability
  EndCoordinator -> Lifecycle : endRoundWithWinnerResolver(input, callback)
  Lifecycle -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE; recheck Active/current/version
  Lifecycle -> WinnerResolver : callback(roundId) inside transaction
  WinnerResolver -> DB : read canonical Round Submissions by acceptedOrder
  DB --> WinnerResolver : earliest Submission or none
  WinnerResolver --> Lifecycle : Result candidate or null
  Lifecycle -> DB : commit Ended + stateVersion + Result/replacement
  DB --> Lifecycle : committed snapshot/result
  Lifecycle --> Foundation : publish after commit
  Foundation --> UI : existing session:state:changed (Ended)
  EndCoordinator --> Teacher : committed SessionStateSnapshot
else End gets SQLite write lock first
  Teacher -> EndCoordinator : endRound(input, trusted ActorContext)
  EndCoordinator -> EndCoordinator : verify teacher scope + round:end capability
  EndCoordinator -> Lifecycle : endRoundWithWinnerResolver(input, callback)
  Lifecycle -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE; recheck Active/current/version
  Lifecycle -> WinnerResolver : callback(roundId) inside transaction
  WinnerResolver -> DB : read canonical Round Submissions by acceptedOrder
  DB --> WinnerResolver : current earliest Submission or none
  WinnerResolver --> Lifecycle : Result candidate or null
  Lifecycle -> DB : commit Ended + stateVersion + Result/replacement
  DB --> Lifecycle : committed snapshot/result
  Lifecycle --> Foundation : publish after commit
  Foundation --> UI : existing session:state:changed (Ended)
  EndCoordinator --> Teacher : committed SessionStateSnapshot
  Student -> StudentApi : later submission attempt
  StudentApi -> DB : validate current Round is Active
  DB --> StudentApi : Round is Ended; reject without write
  StudentApi --> UI : 409 INVALID_PHASE
end
note over EndCoordinator,DB
Teacher makes one synchronous internal End call. Foundation owns the synchronous outer transaction;
the synchronous Student callback returns only the winner candidate. No Promise is awaited inside it.
Resolver/SQL failure rolls back and skips publish.
With no Submission, Foundation creates no Result and clears prior logical-target Result.
All services use the same Database object; Commit precedes async Socket.IO dispatch;
notification delivery is never awaited inside the transaction. No Foundation↔Student import cycle exists.
end note

== Student result projection ==
UI -> StudentApi : GET Student result after Ended
StudentApi -> DB : verify membership; read persisted Result/winning Team/answer rows
DB --> StudentApi : winner data only or no winner
StudentApi --> UI : winner Team name + successful answers, or winner=null
note over StudentApi,UI
Losing submissions and acceptedOrder are never returned.
Foundation ResultView and state event payloads are unchanged.
end note
@enduml
